**Unsafe type cast bypasses runtime validation of workflow_question payload** (data integrity / runtime crash risk)

`workflowQuestion()` validates only that `questionId` is a string, then casts the entire payload via `p as unknown as WorkflowQuestionPayload`. The downstream `WorkflowQuestionPayload` type requires `workflowId: string`, `question: string`, and types `options?: string[]`, `why?: string`, `nodeTitle?: string`, `assumption?: string` — none of these are checked. If the backend ever returns a malformed payload (wrong/missing `workflowId`, `options` not an array, etc.), the component will:

1. Throw at render when `q.options` is read as an array (`Array.isArray` guards `options` only — `q.question`, `q.why`, `q.nodeTitle`, `q.assumption`, `q.workflowId` are read directly), OR
2. Send a malformed body to `workflow_question_respond` via `respondWorkflowQuestion`.

Compare to the other helpers (`memoryIds`, `evolutionProposalId`, `artifactBatch`) which explicitly narrow each field — apply the same pattern here, e.g.:

```ts
function workflowQuestion(n: NotificationItem): WorkflowQuestionPayload | null {
  const p = n.payload;
  if (!p || typeof p.questionId !== "string" || typeof p.workflowId !== "string" || typeof p.question !== "string") return null;
  return p as WorkflowQuestionPayload; // safe after narrow
}
```

…or keep the `unknown` cast but narrow every field you read.

