**`KIND_META[n.kind]` has no runtime fallback for unknown kinds** (runtime crash risk)

`NotificationItem["kind"]` is a TypeScript union, but the union is enforced only at compile time. If the backend ever serializes a new/legacy `kind` value not in `KIND_META`, `meta` becomes `undefined` and the JSX below dereferences `meta.label` (in `aria-label`) and `meta.icon` (in `<span>{meta.icon}</span>`), throwing `Cannot read properties of undefined`.

This is exactly the same risk pattern that `workflowQuestion`, `memoryIds`, `evolutionProposalId`, and `artifactBatch` already mitigate via early-return / null checks. The render loop should do the same — skip the card or render a generic fallback when `meta` is missing:

```tsx
const meta = KIND_META[n.kind];
if (!meta) return null;
return ( <article ... /> );
```

…or use `KIND_META[n.kind] ?? { icon: <Bell size={15} aria-hidden />, label: n.kind }` as a defensive default.

